\name{cellucid_figure_export_get}
\alias{cellucid_figure_export_get}
\title{Read the figure export settings}
\usage{
cellucid_figure_export_get(viewer)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns what it read: a list of \code{auto_text_size} (Set the text in the sizes journals print figure text at: 7 pt, ticks and centroid labels 6 pt, the title 8 pt (font_sizes is then null)), \code{background} (The background: the viewer's, white, transparent or custom), \code{background_color} (The custom background color, lowercase #rrggbb), \code{depth_sort} (Draw 3D points back to front), \code{download} (What Export downloads), \code{dpi} (The resolution of a PNG: its pixels are the width in inches times this (an SVG is the same size, as vectors)), \code{emphasize_selection} (Fade the cells that are not highlighted), \code{export_all_views} (Export every view of the multiview, side by side: each panel is titled by its view's name (view_rename; a view with none by its field and filters)), \code{font_family} (The font of every text), \code{font_sizes} (Text sizes in points (1/72 inch; halves allowed) while auto_text_size is off, else null. They keep their printed size at any width and resolution), \code{frame} (The part of the view exported (needs the preview on), or null for the whole view), \code{include_axes} (Draw the axes), \code{include_legend} (Draw the legend), \code{legend_position} (Where the legend goes), \code{optimized_target_count} (How many points an optimized SVG keeps), \code{preview} (The preview in the panel and the color-vision deficiency it simulates; with the preview on, view.picture with source "export" draws that simulation too (Export writes the true colors)), \code{reference_grid} (Draw a reference grid), \code{selection_muted_opacity} (The opacity of the faded cells, 0 to 1), \code{show_orientation} (Draw the 3D orientation indicator), \code{size_preset} (The figure's width as a journal column: single-column (89 mm), one-and-half-column (120 mm), double-column (183 mm); custom is the width given. A preset sets width), \code{svg_strategy} (How an SVG draws its points: full-vector (the default: every point a circle, editable; a file grows with the cells drawn), optimized-vector (fewer points, optimized_target_count), hybrid (the points as one image, text and axes as vector: small at any cell count)), \code{title} (The figure title while it does not follow the dataset, else null), \code{title_follows_dataset} (The title is the dataset's name (title is then null)), \code{width} (The figure's width in millimetres; the figure is exactly this wide, at every resolution, and as tall as its plots make it (each keeps its view's shape, or its frame's: set a frame to change the shape). A width that is not a preset's makes size_preset custom), \code{x_label} (The x axis label), \code{y_label} (The y axis label). Cells in it are original positions (0-based rows of the dataset's obs).
}
\description{
The Figure export panel's settings now, each named as figure-export.set names it: what Export would write, and what a session or the history put back.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{figure-export.get} (Settings). It reads, and changes nothing: it makes no step of the history.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_figure_export_get(viewer)
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for what it read.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
}
